- Yeah. And so it can cause even downtime.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:55.400
So until recently,
I always said this keeping in mind that

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:02.160
temporary tables are bad
in two areas for me. First is

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:07.680
they're actually really hard to diagnose
because you don't see them. Transaction-

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.840
- Mm
- session which created it does see it.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:15.500
But if, if you're a DBA, like,
trying to... or you have an agent trying

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.971
to diagnose things, connecting to database
